  "id": "Compound::DB06702 - Gene::1132",
  "verbalization": "Fesoterodine is likely to interact with Chrm4 through a shared pathway involving G-protein coupled receptors. The evidence suggests that Fesoterodine binds to Chrm5, which participates in G-protein coupled acetylcholine receptor activity or muscarinic acetylcholine receptor activity, both of which are involved in the activation of Chrm4. This indicates a potential mechanism where Fesoterodine modulates Chrm4 via its interaction with Chrm5, which in turn activates downstream signaling through G-protein coupled receptors. The consistent involvement of Chrm5 in multiple receptor activity pathways supports a unified mechanism, though the exact nature of the interaction between Fesoterodine and Chrm5 remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence suggests a plausible link between Fesoterodine and Chrm4, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction and functional role.",
